course: dictionary
lesson: 4277
title: Water birds: the grebe
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A grebe is a water bird that dives under the water to find its food. You can use context to work out the meaning. «A dabchick is the little grebe, a small bird that dives for its food.» The sentence tells you that a dabchick and a little grebe are the same bird, and that it dives for food.
explain: The clues «lakes and rivers» tell you where grebes live. A grebe is at home on the water, not on land. Ask yourself what fits the sentence, then check that your meaning still makes sense.
explain: Some grebes have fancy feathers. The great crested grebe has a crest of feathers on its head, and it is famous for its courtship dance. In this dance a pair rise up breast to breast and shake their heads.
fact: A grebe is a diving water bird with lobed toes and a sharp beak.
fact: Grebes live on lakes and rivers, in the UK, Ireland, North America, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «Grebe» is a noun. One is a grebe, and more than one are grebes.
fact: The great crested grebe has fancy feathers on its head.
exercise: «A dabchick is the little grebe, a small bird that dives for its food.» What is a dabchick? | A moorhen | *A little grebe | A fish | A kingfisher
exercise: What does a grebe do to find its food? | It digs a tunnel in the bank | It sits still on a branch | Flies high above the trees | *It dives under the water
exercise: The great crested grebe is famous for its courtship «dance». What happens in the dance? | A race across the lake | The birds dig a tunnel in the bank | A bird sings from the top of a tree | *A pair rise up breast to breast and shake their heads
test: Where do grebes live? | In deep forests far from water | In the desert | On the tops of mountains | *On lakes and rivers
test: Which word describes a grebe's toes? | Hairy | *Lobed | Long and thin like a stick | Sharp like a hook
exam: «The little grebe dives for its food.» Using the context, what does dives mean? | *Goes head first under the water | Sits still on a branch | Sings a loud song | Flies high into the sky
